{
  "name": "mcp-rust-sdk",
  "description": "The official Rust implementation of the Model Context Protocol (MCP), providing a comprehensive, asynchronous SDK built on the Tokio runtime. It enables the development of both MCP clients and servers with support for a wide array of transports including stdio, Server-Sent Events (SSE), TCP, and WASI. The project features sophisticated procedural macros for declarative tool and prompt routing, alongside robust support for resource elicitation, structured outputs, and OAuth2-based authentication.",
